  <h2 id="bpday">A day in each field, in plain terms</h2>

  <p>
    A biotechnology day in a lab or plant often starts with checking cultures, instruments and yesterday's readings. The middle of the day goes to running a method and recording every step, and the end goes to cleaning, labelling and writing up what happened.
  </p>
  <p>
    A pharmacy day centres on prescriptions, stock, labelling and talking to people about how to use a medicine. Accuracy in reading a prescription and counting stock matters more than speed, and records are checked by inspectors.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ask yourself which of the two days feels less tiring after a week of imagining it.
  </p>

